-# locals: src (String), alt (String), width, height and placeholder (optional,
-# the preview's size and blurred stand-in from the Work read)
-#
-# The record's preview image. `alt` names the work rather than describing the
-# picture, because nothing in the repository holds a description of what a
-# preview depicts — the title is the one true thing we can say about it. It is
-# worded as a preview so a screen reader announces something distinct from the
-# heading beside it, instead of repeating the title twice.
-#
-# Eager and high priority because this is usually the page's LCP element:
-# `loading: lazy` holds the request until layout, which is the delay LCP counts.
-#
-# The stand-in is the <img>'s own background, so the picture paints over it in
-# the same box with no swap. Do not add a transition (docs/design.md).
%img.mt-1{fetchpriority: "high", src: src, alt: alt, **preview_image_attributes(local_assigns[:width], local_assigns[:height], local_assigns[:placeholder])}/
